bonds and different

59
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:22,300
hydrocarbon chain configurations
to stabilize their

60
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,440
membranes, as opposed to
using a secondary molecule.

61
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:30,620
The cell walls between fungi
and bacteria are different

62
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:33,860
too. Where we see a
wall composed mainly of

63
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:37,380
peptidoglycan and bacteria,
fungi instead contain the

64
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:41,910
polysaccharide chitin,
which is a long chain of N

65
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:46,280
-acetylglucosamine, or NAG,
and is chemically identical

66
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:49,900
to the NAG found in
peptidoglycan, with the latter of

67
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:53,100
those two molecules also
containing the sugar NAM.

68
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:56,260
Chitin is also a pretty
versatile molecule,

69
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:59,060
and it's used as
the basis for the

70
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:01,580
exoskeletons of insects
and crustaceans.

71
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,280
Fungal cell walls also
contain other polysaccharides

72
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,600
as well, the most
important of which is

73
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:11,780
glucan that's made up of
long polymers of glucose.

74
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:18,520
Fungi are found everywhere
in all different environments

75
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,220
and can be seen in two
basic morphological

76
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:25,320
types. Yeast that grow as
single cells and reproduce

77
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:28,980
