mat called a mycelium

80
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:39,860
Now the medically important
fungal species that

81
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:42,870
we're going to cover
today Also display

82
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:46,720
thermodimorphism as a
virulence factor Meaning that

83
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:49,720
they will exist as molds
in the environment at

84
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:52,440
ambient temperature but
then they'll grow as

85
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:55,820
yeast in human body tissue
at body temperature.

86
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:59,680
Now, generally speaking,
with very few exceptions,

87
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:02,440
most fungi can't grow
at body temperature.

88
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:06,220
37 degrees is usually
too high, and they prefer

89
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:09,000
room temperature around
20 to 25 degrees,

90
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,840
which is why fungal
infections are usually more

91
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,720
