death in very extreme cases.

157
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:08,240
Systemic mycoses are
endemic infections that are

158
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:10,760
geographically restricted,
as you can see on the

159
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:14,440
map here, with three fungi
causing infections in

160
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:18,220
the u.s histoplasma and
blastomyces are found in the

161
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:21,530
majority of the eastern
and central u.s along

162
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:25,860
with histoplasma in the
texas region and coccidioides

163
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:28,220
confine more to the
american southwest and

164
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:32,560
california there's also
a fourth paracoccidioides

165
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:35,700
indicated by the star here
that's not seen in the u.s

166
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:38,620
but rather is found in
central and south america

167
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:44,330
okay so we'll start
here with the disease

168
00:09:44,330 --> 00:09:48,300
coccidioideomycosis which is
the clinical manifestation

169
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:52,700
of infections with either
coccidioides posidaceae

170
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:57,400
or imidus now the disease
is the same but the

171
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:00,560
distribution of the two
species is slightly different

172
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:03,840
both are endemic in
arid regions in the

173
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:07,200
southwestern united states
and northern Mexico but

174
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,880
imidus is going to be
found more in California.

175
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:13,260
Both naturally inhabit the soil

176
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:16,900
where they grow as
hyphae with rectangular

177
00:10:16,970 --> 00:10:19,960
fragments of the hyphae
that are going to be able to

178
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:22,780
act as spores like you
could see in the image

179
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:25,850
here and those are referred
